  "body": "Closes #425\nClaim: cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/fb-quickwins-reviewer-opus)\n\n### What was checked\n#1059 (merged as 995dbd80) put the account button, top left with the avatar, on the five tab roots. Not done: a category's topic list, a pushed screen. Legacy shows back, then the account avatar there (`MainWindow.swift:803-818` @ 87fe0d1c; operator comment of 2026-11-14 on #425).\n\n### Problem\nA category's topic list (Catégories content column, and the category opened from a Favoris section title) has no account button.\n\n### Change\n- `TopicListView.showsAccountMenu` (off by default) adds `AccountMenuButton` at `.topBarLeading`, drawn after the back button. `TopicsColumn.showsAccountMenu` passes it through.\n- On: Catégories' topic column (only when the split is collapsed: at regular width, e.g. a foldable's inner screen, the category list column already has the button, round 1 finding 1) and the category pushed from Favoris. Off: the Favoris root (its tab already adds the button).\n- Not touched: the iPad sidebar's topic lists (`CategoriesSidebarColumn`; legacy has the avatar in the iPad list column, `MainWindow.swift:1932-1938`: to port or track on #893), and Plus (the operator's \"remove from Plus\" is marked *to confirm* on #425).\n- `CategoriesTabView` takes an optional initial column, so a test can start on the topic column.\n\n### Tests\n`AccountMenuPlacementTests`: `aPushedCategoryTopicListHasTheAccountButtonOnlyWhenAsked` (true/false, negative control) and `theCategoryTopicListsOfTheTabsHaveExactlyOneAccountButton` (`CategoriesTabView` with `selectedSource`, `FavoritesTabView` with `openedCategory`, compact window; exactly one leading item, so removing the flag at a call site or doubling it fails). Not run here (Linux); `compile-check` runs on the head.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-009\nLegacy ref: MainWindow.swift:235-262; MainToolbar.swift:57-64; MainWindow.swift:803-818 @ 87fe0d1c\nSwiftHFR final: Avatar menu, top left, on the five tab roots and, on the iPhone, after the back button of a category's topic list (#425, #1059); the iPad sidebar's topic lists have none yet (#893); manage-accounts entry added; Plus keeps it pending the operator's call.\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CDvQG8jqNrseTphdnF",
